# 3. Core Architectural Principles

## Principle 01 — Frontend Is Not Canonical State

The frontend never becomes the authoritative owner of:

- project state
- task state
- milestone state
- risk state
- assessment results
- blueprint state
- AI execution state
- authorization
- permissions

The backend/database owns canonical state.

The frontend displays and interacts with it.

---

## Principle 02 — Domain Ownership

Every meaningful capability must have an identifiable owner.

Examples:

```text
Task functionality          → Task domain
Project functionality       → Project domain
Notification functionality  → Notification domain
Authentication              → Auth domain
AI execution presentation   → AI domain
```

Avoid generic business-logic dumping grounds such as:

```text
misc/
helpers/
stuff/
common-business-logic/
```

---

## Principle 03 — Shared Means Truly Shared

A component becomes shared only when it is genuinely reusable.

Do not prematurely move everything into `shared/`.

---

## Principle 04 — Role-Specific Behavior Remains Role-Specific

```text
Student functionality
≠
Mentor functionality
≠
Admin functionality
```

The roles may consume common domain primitives, but their experiences remain distinct.

---

## Principle 05 — Backend Remains Authoritative

```text
Frontend permission check
        ↓
UX

Backend authorization
        ↓
Security
```

---

# 4. High-Level Frontend Architecture

```text
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                 GrowFlow UI                   │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│               Application Layer               │
│ Routing / Providers / Shell / Auth Bootstrap  │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│              Experience Layer                 │
│ Student / Mentor / Admin / Public Experiences │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                Domain Layer                   │
│ Projects / Tasks / AI / Groups / Documents   │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│              Shared UI Layer                  │
│ Buttons / Tables / Forms / Modals / Charts   │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│             Infrastructure Layer              │
│ API / SSE / Auth / Storage / Logging         │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

The architecture is defined by responsibility and dependency direction, not merely by folders.

---

# 5. Dependency Direction

The primary dependency model is:

```text
Application
    ↓
Experience
    ↓
Domain
    ↓
Shared UI / Infrastructure
```

Infrastructure handles technical communication and mechanisms. It must not contain GrowFlow business decisions.

For example:

- An API client knows how to make a request.
- An SSE client knows how to receive events.
- Neither should decide the canonical meaning of project health, risk, or lifecycle state.

---

# 6. Frontend Architectural Layers

## 6.1 Application Layer

Responsible for application bootstrapping:

- routing
- providers
- authentication initialization
- authorization initialization
- application shell
- global error boundaries
- global configuration
- application-level event handling

It should not contain domain business logic.

---

## 6.2 Experience Layer

Represents user experiences:

```text
Public
Auth
Student
Mentor
Admin
```

The experience layer composes domain functionality.

It should not duplicate domain logic.

---

## 6.3 Domain Layer

The domain layer owns meaningful frontend capabilities.

Potential domain modules:

```text
auth
users
projects
project-definitions
project-instances
assessment
blueprint
tasks
milestones
risks
roadmap
documents
github
activity
groups
help-requests
mentor-feedback
notifications
search
ai
rag
analytics
system-health
audit
sharing
```

Not every domain requires an identical internal directory structure. Structure follows responsibility.

---

## 6.4 Shared UI Layer

Shared UI contains presentation primitives such as:

```text
Button
Input
Select
Dialog
Drawer
Tabs
Table
Card
Badge
Tooltip
Dropdown
Pagination
Skeleton
EmptyState
ErrorState
LoadingState
DatePicker
CommandPalette
```

Shared components should be:

- role-neutral
- domain-neutral where possible
- accessible
- reusable
- visually consistent

---

## 6.5 Infrastructure Layer

Infrastructure handles technical communication and mechanisms:

```text
REST client
SSE client
authentication adapter
storage adapter
logging
telemetry
configuration
request handling
error normalization
```

Infrastructure must not become a business-logic layer.

